WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.

5
00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office Rewatch podcast just for you.

6
00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

7
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.550
We're The Office ladies.

8
00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:25.390
All right, everybody.

9
00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:27.390
We are still saying goodbye to Toby.

10
00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:30.470
It is Goodbye, Toby, Part 2.

11
00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:33.430
It's a long goodbye, but he deserves it.

12
00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:35.030
He's been at the company a long time.

13
00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:36.330
He deserves a two-parter.

14
00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:38.850
Michael's going to give him a big send-off, lady.

15
00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:40.050
He sure is.

16
00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:48.410
Guys, it's Season 4, Episode 19, written by Jen Salata and Paul Lieberstein, directed by Paul Feig.

17
00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:52.310
Here is a summary of Part 2 of Goodbye, Toby.

18
00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:53.090
Okay.

19
00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:59.850
An extravagant goodbye party is being thrown in the parking lot for Toby.

20
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:02.730
Ryan is arrested for fraud.

21
00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:05.770
Michael discovers big news about Jan.

22
00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:10.810
Jim plans to propose to Pam, but gets upstaged by Andy.

23
00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:13.410
And Phyllis discovers a secret.

24
00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:15.190
Does she ever?

25
00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:18.770
All right.

26
00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:19.950
Jumping right in.

27
00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:21.410
Fast fact number one.

28
00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:23.590
I'm calling this Party Time.

29
00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:26.490
Are you going to give me a breakdown of all the party?

30
00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:28.050
You know I am.

31
00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:32.570
We got fan questions from Abby M and Yvette M.

32
00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:36.770
How many days did it take to film Toby's goodbye party?

33
00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:39.210
How long did it take to set it up?

34
00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:41.450
Well, you know I went to Kentopedia.

35
00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:48.050
He said it took one full day to set it up and two days and nights to film.

36
00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:53.310
We filmed April 17th and 18th of 2008.

37
00:01:53.970 --> 00:02:02.390
The Ferris wheel came from a company called Awesome Events, and it cost us $7,500 to rent

38
00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:04.170
that Ferris wheel for three days.

39
00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:05.310
Dang.

40
00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:06.190
Mm-hmm.

41
00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:08.530
That's a pricey Ferris wheel.

42
00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:11.510
Here's what I remember about those party scenes, Angela.

43
00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:14.410
It was very hot during the day.

44
00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:16.210
And then at night, it got cold.

45
00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:16.850
Yeah.

46
00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:20.270
I remember I had hand warmers in my pockets at night.

47
00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:25.230
And you know when you go skiing and you put those toe warmers in your ski boots?

48
00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:28.310
I had those in my shoes for the night shoot.

49
00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:32.290
Also, whenever they didn't see our feet, we had Uggs on.

50
00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:36.470
And Jenna, I have an Ugg catch later in this episode.

51
00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:38.270
Whose Uggs do you see?

52
00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:39.550
Not going to tell.

53
00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:43.890
Guys, you're going to have to wait for it.

54
00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:45.990
She's making you wait for it.

55
00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:52.650
But also, in between takes, do you remember our wardrobe department had these big, puffy

56
00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:57.150
coats, like the kind that go down to your ankles, giant puffy coats, and they would bring

57
00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:02.850
them out to us so that we could put them on in between takes outside when we were cold.

58
00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:04.190
And you know what?

59
00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:05.010
What?

60
00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:06.670
I still have mine.

61
00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:07.770
You do?

62
00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:09.330
Oh, what a score.

63
00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:10.050
Yeah.

64
00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:15.850
And on the label, on the inside of the coat, it says Pam, written in Sharpie.

65
00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:16.890
Aww.

66
00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:19.770
Because that's how they knew whose coat belonged to who.

67
00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:20.590
They Sharpied it.

68
00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:22.930
Well, these were like giant sleeping bags.

69
00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:23.470
Yes.

70
00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:24.650
Made into jackets.

71
00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:26.270
Well described.

72
00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:29.130
Okay, fast fact number two.

73
00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:30.930
I'm kind of sad.

74
00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:32.470
I know.

75
00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:34.690
This is not just goodbye, Toby.

76
00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:35.670
Nope.

77
00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:37.910
This is goodbye, Kentopedia.

78
00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:39.070
Yes.

79
00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:40.450
Kent Svornak.

80
00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:42.790
This was the end of his run on the office.

81
00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:43.570
Yeah.

82
00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.810
After this, he moved on.

83
00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:53.730
And he became the producer and production manager for Anger Management, Dear White People,

84
00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:56.230
and most recently, The Conners.

85
00:03:56.790 --> 00:04:00.910
He is an amazing, amazing production manager, you guys.

86
00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:03.110
We were so lucky to have him for four seasons.

87
00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:09.070
And Office Ladies has been so lucky that he saved like everything.

88
00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:11.250
Talk about digital hoarder.

89
00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:14.310
Kentopedia is giving you a run for your money, Angela.

90
00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:15.970
Well, I think he's beat me.

91
00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:17.250
But I just love him.

92
00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:20.070
And we loved him so much.

93
00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:25.930
Jenna, in anticipation of this being his last episode, I went through and found all of these

94
00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:28.970
emails during this week that I traded with Kent.

95
00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:31.250
This was like towards the end of my pregnancy.

96
00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:37.290
And he and I were having to schedule a lot of things around my OBGYN appointments and everything.

97
00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:42.930
And if I could share anything with you guys is the kindness and the thoughtfulness that this

98
00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:47.990
man had for every member of the cast and making the show the best it could be.

99
00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:51.410
And we were so sad to see him go.

100
00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:53.030
I just love this guy.

101
00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:54.250
I love him, too.

102
00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:56.250
And I love being in touch with him.

103
00:04:56.390 --> 00:04:57.990
And he was so great to us on The Office.

104
00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:00.030
And he's been so great to us on Office Ladies.

105
00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:01.470
We love you, Kentopedia.

106
00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:03.410
We love you, Kentopedia.

107
00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:07.070
And I'm going to share a few of our emails later in this episode.

108
00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:13.250
Angela, I want to share one of my favorite fun facts about Kent as we say goodbye to him.

109
00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:14.170
Okay, what?

110
00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:20.670
In his youth, Kent was an assistant to the creator of Golden Girls.

111
00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:27.630
Her name is Susan Harris, and she loved Kent's last name so much that when she wrote Golden

112
00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:32.550
Girls, she named Bea Arthur's character Dorothy Zabornak.

113
00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:34.110
Amazing!

114
00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:35.170
Yes!

115
00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:37.770
He was the inspiration behind that name.

116
00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:41.530
He told me he was beyond excited by this honor.

117
00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:43.430
He was like, I mean, who wouldn't be?

118
00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:47.790
And then he went on to be the first assistant director on Golden Girls.

119
00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:51.050
And he said Bea Arthur was like a second mother to him.

120
00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:52.150
He just loved her.

121
00:05:52.730 --> 00:05:54.410
That is so wonderful.

122
00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:55.770
I love all of that.

123
00:05:56.030 --> 00:05:56.910
We love you, Kent.

124
00:05:57.910 --> 00:05:59.930
Okay, rounding out my fast facts.

125
00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:01.330
Fast fact number three.

126
00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:04.630
Angela, you came up with this idea, and I just loved it.

127
00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:08.210
I think we should do it for every character.

128
00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:10.250
And now I'm like, oh, we might have missed a few.

129
00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:14.550
We might have to, in a revisited, do this for other characters.

130
00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:15.630
That's right.

131
00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:17.270
Here's what we're talking about.

132
00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:22.670
Angela said, whenever we say goodbye to a character, we should give them a show Bible

133
00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:23.030
goodbye.

134
00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:29.130
So I went through the show Bible, and I gathered facts about Toby Flunderson.

135
00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:29.770
Yay!

136
00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:31.750
Here they are.

137
00:06:32.170 --> 00:06:37.430
Toby Flunderson, graduate of Bishop O'Hara High School, class of 89.

138
00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:44.510
He is divorced, but his wife is still his emergency contact, although her last name is Becker now.

139
00:06:44.510 --> 00:06:45.550
Hmm.

140
00:06:46.190 --> 00:06:52.790
During his 12 years working HR at Dunder Mifflin, he has explained female anatomy to Dwight, told

141
00:06:52.790 --> 00:06:57.530
Kevin he should ditch Dunder Mifflin's health care plan and get on his fiancee Stacy's plan

142
00:06:57.530 --> 00:06:59.730
instead because it's definitely going to be better.

143
00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:06.450
He sent out a memo regarding Jim and Pam's PDA, and he attended Jan's deposition and was

144
00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:08.350
present for the reading of Michael's diary.

145
00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:11.710
Toby is one of the founding members of the Finer Things Club.

146
00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:17.290
He bought Angela her baby jazz poster, and he can run a mile in seven minutes.

147
00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:22.550
He's been trying to flirt with Pam and ask her out ever since season three.

148
00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:26.290
That is also how long he's been talking about going to Costa Rica.

149
00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:30.690
He started talking about that ever since he heard the Scranton branch might be closing.

150
00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:36.250
And now, after a very awkward moment of rubbing Pam's knee, he is finally leaving.

151
00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:39.530
Although, guys, he is going to come back.

152
00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:40.250
Spoiler alert.

153
00:07:40.530 --> 00:07:41.490
Oh, I love that.

154
00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:43.210
I love the show Bible goodbye.

155
00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:44.890
Show Bible goodbye.

156
00:07:45.050 --> 00:07:46.610
It's like a show Bible eulogy.

157
00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:47.510
Mm-hmm.

158
00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:48.250
A little bit.

159
00:07:48.490 --> 00:07:52.770
Well, we'll definitely have to do that for a few characters in a Revisited, like for Karen

160
00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:53.310
Filipelli.

161
00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:55.230
Oh, yeah.

162
00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:56.670
That's got to be in a Revisited.

163
00:07:56.930 --> 00:07:57.730
We'll do it.

164
00:07:57.910 --> 00:07:59.350
That is all I have, Angela.

165
00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:01.150
Quick fast facts today.

166
00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:02.270
I like it.

167
00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:07.130
I have some fun stuff from the shooting draft, but maybe before we get into this episode,

168
00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:08.110
we should take a little break.

169
00:08:08.290 --> 00:08:12.350
Let's take a little break, but I've got a lot to say about this one, so we might be

170
00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:14.950
short here up on top, but we're going to be long later.

171
00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:17.970
That's what she said?

172
00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:19.350
Is that a thing she said?

173
00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:20.190
Maybe.

174
00:08:20.590 --> 00:08:20.950
Maybe.

175
00:08:21.190 --> 00:08:21.870
I don't know.

176
00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:23.570
You decide over the break.

177
00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:24.110
Okay.

178
00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:35.120
All right.

179
00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:39.120
We are back, and Michael is so excited to have his moment.

180
00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:42.020
It is time for Toby's exit interview.

181
00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.200
Michael shows up with a gift.

182
00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:45.680
It's wrapped.

183
00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:46.580
There's a ribbon.

184
00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:47.360
Yeah.

185
00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:49.000
He walks in the conference room with Toby.

186
00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:49.920
He shuts the door.

187
00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:53.000
He's ready to get started, but then what happens?

188
00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:54.480
He says this.

189
00:08:54.700 --> 00:09:01.600
Can I just say that of all the idiots, in all the idiot villages, in all the idiot worlds,

190
00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:04.860
you stand alone, my friend.

191
00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:12.260
And then right as he's about to really go off, Holly enters, and he's like, oh, hey.

192
00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:15.680
And she's like, yeah, I've got to be here.

193
00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:16.500
This is part of my job.

194
00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:17.260
And he's like, no, no, no.

195
00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:18.520
Shouldn't you just tour some more?

196
00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:19.440
Go see the bailer.

197
00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:21.000
She goes, maybe later.

198
00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:22.620
This is actually part of my job.

199
00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:23.820
And then Pam walks in.

200
00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:25.520
She's like, do you need me to take notes?

201
00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:27.040
Toby's all over it.

202
00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:27.780
Toby's like, stay.

203
00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:28.540
Pam, stay.

204
00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:29.640
She's like, all right.

205
00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:32.740
Well, this is now not going as Michael had planned.

206
00:09:32.740 --> 00:09:34.480
He gets out his note cards.

207
00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:37.700
He's written some questions.

208
00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:41.000
Again, Steve Carell should have won 15 Emmys.

209
00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:41.880
I mean, come on.

210
00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:42.300
Yeah.

211
00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:48.960
This is his having all this stuff he wanted to just tee off on Toby about and now having

212
00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:53.760
to dial it back and somehow be acceptable in front of this woman he's falling in love

213
00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:57.280
with every moment Steve crushes.

214
00:09:57.440 --> 00:10:01.780
His first question is, who do you think you are?

215
00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:05.660
And Toby goes, I'm Toby.

216
00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:11.300
Now, I hope you noticed in the background, I'm going to toot my own horn.

217
00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:13.060
I am taking notes.

218
00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:14.020
No, I know.

219
00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:16.260
I watched you write it all down.

220
00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:20.440
And I am actually writing down, who are you?

221
00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:22.220
And then I wrote down Toby.

222
00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:25.860
And a couple times I wrote down, he is Toby.

223
00:10:26.720 --> 00:10:30.240
But my whole backstory, and Angela, I loved doing these scenes.

224
00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:36.040
I loved every time Pam's sole purpose in a scene was to take notes because I was just

225
00:10:36.040 --> 00:10:36.860
an audience member.

226
00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:38.080
I got to just sit there.

227
00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:41.140
I didn't have any like real lines I had to say or anything I had to do.

228
00:10:41.380 --> 00:10:43.280
You just had to try not to laugh.

229
00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:44.140
Pretty much.

230
00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:46.680
But I always took diligent notes.

231
00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:47.980
I really did.

232
00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:53.480
Because I liked to pretend that Michael would ask me to transcribe these meetings later.

233
00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:57.540
I like to think he made you go in his office and read the whole thing back to him.

234
00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:59.260
Just so he could feel important.

235
00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:04.400
This was like something he saw in an old movie once that secretaries do for their bosses.

236
00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:05.280
That's right.

237
00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:08.960
His second note card says, what gives you the right?

238
00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:12.860
And this is when Holly steps in.

239
00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:13.580
She's like, you know what?

240
00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:14.400
I brought the binder.

241
00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:16.120
Do you want to use it?

242
00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:17.080
Take a look at it?

243
00:11:17.560 --> 00:11:17.800
Yeah.

244
00:11:18.100 --> 00:11:23.720
And Michael starts to ask Toby if he has any suggestions on ways that, you know, Dunder

245
00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:25.020
Mifflin could improve itself.

246
00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:32.300
And Toby seems like he's going to answer this question until, oh my God, Steve puts his hands

247
00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:35.580
up to his face to shield himself from Holly.

248
00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:38.180
And he gives Toby this look.

249
00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:39.200
It's so good.

250
00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:42.740
He actually mouths the words, I'll kill you.

251
00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:46.800
I missed it.

252
00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:48.720
He says, I'll kill you.

253
00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:54.600
And in the script, it's written that he does the slit the throat, you know, the finger across

254
00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:55.580
the throat gesture.

255
00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:56.080
Yeah.

256
00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:58.620
But I don't know if this was Steve improvising.

257
00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:00.980
I feel like he probably gave them a few different choices.

258
00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:03.920
But the one they picked was him whispering.

259
00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:07.880
It's so amazing.

260
00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:11.380
And Toby just goes, I guess everything's okay.

261
00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:11.460
Okay.

262
00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:12.440
Yeah.

263
00:12:12.740 --> 00:12:17.080
And he's like, you know, he has this moment where he's like, I mean, I made it this far.

264
00:12:17.260 --> 00:12:17.760
Why not?

265
00:12:18.140 --> 00:12:20.740
Well, Pam is going to suggest that Toby open his gift.

266
00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:21.840
Toby, open it.

267
00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:22.660
What is it?

268
00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:24.100
And Michael's like, no, no, no, no, no.

269
00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:24.620
You know what?

270
00:12:26.900 --> 00:12:32.640
You guys, it's a rock with a note on it that says, suck on this.

271
00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:35.720
I watched this episode with Lee.

272
00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:38.580
He laughed so hard at this joke.

273
00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:40.760
He couldn't stop laughing that it was a rock.

274
00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:42.500
He just thought that was so funny.

275
00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:47.660
Michael, you know, acts like he had no idea.

276
00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:50.380
And he's like, who pulled this prank on Toby?

277
00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:51.160
This is horrible.

278
00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:52.860
And Dwight's like, you told me to do it.

279
00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:53.480
And he's like, shh.

280
00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:54.760
And then he goes, you know what this was?

281
00:12:54.920 --> 00:13:00.220
It was a psych, psych, psyched you out because there's a real gift coming.

282
00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:06.000
And this is my second favorite thing to do as Pam after taking notes in a meeting, which

283
00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:08.240
is painting Michael into a corner.

284
00:13:08.780 --> 00:13:11.540
And she says, what's the gift, Michael?

285
00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:12.860
What is it?

286
00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:15.340
Oh, is it your watch?

287
00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:18.340
And he's like, it is.

288
00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:19.340
It is my watch.

289
00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:20.100
How did you know?

290
00:13:20.340 --> 00:13:21.860
And she says, I just knew.

291
00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:23.580
He's so ticked off.

292
00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:25.820
He has to give Toby his watch.

293
00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:26.680
You know what?

294
00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:28.800
That's a genuine Seiko piece.

295
00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:32.620
He's going to have to give Toby the certificate that's framed as well, I guess.

296
00:13:32.900 --> 00:13:33.720
I guess he will.

297
00:13:34.140 --> 00:13:38.780
This delightful scene is interrupted by some hubbub in the bullpen.

298
00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:43.300
Everyone is gathered around Jim's computer watching a YouTube video.

299
00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:49.980
So yeah, Ryan is being arrested and someone has uploaded the moment and they're all watching

300
00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:50.320
it.

301
00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:55.100
I want you guys to know that they actually put that video on YouTube.

302
00:13:55.640 --> 00:13:57.520
It was a private account.

303
00:13:57.840 --> 00:14:00.860
So John is actually watching it during that scene.

304
00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:01.680
We all are.

305
00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:03.300
But it was a private account.

306
00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:08.860
When the episode aired, they made the video go live on YouTube so everyone could watch

307
00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:09.060
it.

308
00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:10.300
Oh, that's so great.

309
00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:11.460
I didn't know that.

310
00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:14.740
Yeah, but Michael is very upset.

311
00:14:15.280 --> 00:14:19.780
He's in his office and Holly is saying to Toby, what do you do in this situation?

312
00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:21.440
Toby says, I don't do anything.

313
00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:22.760
Just leave it alone.

314
00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:24.840
But Holly is amazing.

315
00:14:25.020 --> 00:14:28.220
She goes into Michael's office and she really comforts him.

316
00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:29.220
Michael is crying.

317
00:14:29.520 --> 00:14:30.480
He's really sweet.

318
00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:32.400
He says, I'm worried about my friend.

319
00:14:32.940 --> 00:14:33.120
Yeah.

320
00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:34.540
And she says, that's normal.

321
00:14:34.760 --> 00:14:37.200
You take the time you need to have your feelings.

322
00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:44.280
Which leads to just a wonderful talking head, Angela, that I love, where Michael says, Holly

323
00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:46.600
is sweet and simple like a lady baker.

324
00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:51.440
And he just wouldn't be surprised to find out that she'd worked in a bakery before coming

325
00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:52.380
to Dunder Mifflin.

326
00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:55.720
I mean, he's pretty sure she's baked on a professional level.

327
00:14:56.060 --> 00:14:58.100
Because baking is love, right?

328
00:14:58.440 --> 00:14:58.780
Yeah.

329
00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:00.520
Only sweet ladies bake.

330
00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:02.440
Sweet ladies who take care of you.

331
00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:03.120
Yeah.

332
00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:04.120
Aww.

333
00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:09.380
Well, after this very sweet Michael talking head, we are all going to go out in the parking

334
00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:11.480
lot because the party is starting.

335
00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:12.400
Oh, yeah.

336
00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:17.220
But before we get into that parking lot, Jenna, I need to share a little backstory.

337
00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:18.480
Okay.

338
00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:25.160
Have you ever been on the phone with someone and you actually hear that person go into a

339
00:15:25.160 --> 00:15:26.700
full flop sweat?

340
00:15:27.220 --> 00:15:28.520
Where is this going?

341
00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:30.420
Because I have.

342
00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:31.240
Okay.

343
00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:32.260
I have.

344
00:15:32.420 --> 00:15:34.160
And that person was Kent Zabornak.

345
00:15:34.340 --> 00:15:35.120
Oh, my gosh.

346
00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:36.160
Oh, gosh.

347
00:15:36.320 --> 00:15:40.240
Not only did I remember this, but then I found some emails between Kent and I that really

348
00:15:40.240 --> 00:15:41.060
painted the picture.

349
00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:45.240
And I wanted to share the story with you guys that I almost didn't make it to the parking

350
00:15:45.240 --> 00:15:45.560
lot.

351
00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:47.520
Oh, now I know what you're talking about.

352
00:15:48.040 --> 00:15:55.040
In my emails, I found that on Thursday, April 10th of 2008 at 4 p.m., I had a routine

353
00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:56.840
checkup with my OBGYN.

354
00:15:57.120 --> 00:15:58.360
I emailed Kent about it.

355
00:15:58.360 --> 00:15:59.880
He said, no problem, Ange.

356
00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:02.920
We'll have you wrapped in time to make it to that doctor's appointment.

357
00:16:03.380 --> 00:16:08.380
So, lady, while I was at my doctor's appointment, you know, how they sort of check all your vitals

358
00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:09.100
and do everything.

359
00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:15.300
And I had had, like, I was feeling like a little bit of cramping, but nothing I was really

360
00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:15.860
worried about.

361
00:16:15.860 --> 00:16:19.400
And she was like, Angela, you're having contractions.

362
00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:20.640
And I said, what?

363
00:16:20.920 --> 00:16:21.980
And she said, yeah.

364
00:16:22.220 --> 00:16:24.900
And she immediately sent me to the hospital.

365
00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:26.480
From your doctor's appointment?

366
00:16:26.700 --> 00:16:28.740
From my doctor's appointment at 4 o'clock.

367
00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:29.900
Now I'm in the hospital.

368
00:16:30.100 --> 00:16:32.720
I'm having contractions every five minutes.

369
00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:39.300
And around 6 o'clock in the evening, Jenny O'Keefe, who was our second AD, called me to

370
00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:41.240
tell me my call time, right?

371
00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:42.520
For the next day.

372
00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:43.220
For the next day.

373
00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:46.040
She's like, hi, Angela, your call time tomorrow is 530 a.m.

374
00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:47.680
And I said, Jenny, I'm in the hospital.

375
00:16:48.340 --> 00:16:49.320
She said, what?

376
00:16:49.640 --> 00:16:51.760
And I said, I'm having contractions.

377
00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:53.280
And she goes, okay, okay.

378
00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:56.320
Um, I will, uh, get back to you.

379
00:16:56.800 --> 00:17:00.880
Literally three seconds later, my phone rings and it's Kent Sabornak.

380
00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:04.800
And I will never forget the first thing he said to me.

381
00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:09.260
He said, hey, hey, Ange, uh, we having this baby today?

382
00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:12.360
But like his voice cracked and went up.

383
00:17:12.480 --> 00:17:14.180
It's like, we having this baby today?

384
00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:18.840
Because what you guys have to know is they were building a freaking Ferris wheel in the

385
00:17:18.840 --> 00:17:19.420
parking lot.

386
00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:20.440
That's right.

387
00:17:20.440 --> 00:17:25.760
And to give you guys some context, this was all happening about three weeks before your

388
00:17:25.760 --> 00:17:26.760
due date, right?

389
00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:27.120
Yeah.

390
00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:29.840
We just had a few more days of filming with you.

391
00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:34.640
Everyone just assumed that we would finish this episode and then you would go off on

392
00:17:34.640 --> 00:17:37.180
your summer hiatus and have your baby.

393
00:17:37.980 --> 00:17:39.560
Kent thought he had time.

394
00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:44.640
But in reality, you are in the hospital and he was probably standing in the parking lot as

395
00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:47.700
they're assembling this Ferris wheel and he's freaking out.

396
00:17:48.220 --> 00:17:48.580
Yeah.

397
00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:52.040
How does Andy propose if Angela can't be there?

398
00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:52.620
Yeah.

399
00:17:53.180 --> 00:17:54.660
In front of the Ferris wheel.

400
00:17:55.320 --> 00:17:56.900
So I said, Kent, I don't know.

401
00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:58.460
I don't know if I'm having this baby tonight.

402
00:17:58.600 --> 00:18:00.940
And he said, well, would you keep me posted?

403
00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:02.360
And I said, sure.

404
00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:05.180
And it turned out to be false labor.

405
00:18:05.380 --> 00:18:06.960
I was there till about two in the morning.

406
00:18:07.180 --> 00:18:09.520
I did have to go work a half day the next day.

407
00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:13.900
And let me tell you, Kent had already hired a stunt woman.

408
00:18:14.120 --> 00:18:15.540
Her name was Melissa Barker.

409
00:18:15.640 --> 00:18:19.180
And she was to be my body double for the rest of this shoot.

410
00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:23.880
They really wanted to try to make sure I did not have to work if I was not in a speaking

411
00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:24.820
scene, right?

412
00:18:25.020 --> 00:18:26.000
They would use Melissa.

413
00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:30.360
Angela, it was so weird to have her on set because she was dressed just like you.

414
00:18:30.480 --> 00:18:32.120
She had her hair done just like you.

415
00:18:32.120 --> 00:18:34.840
From behind, she seriously looked like you.

416
00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:40.420
So yes, if there was a scene in the conference room and you were just not speaking, she would

417
00:18:40.420 --> 00:18:43.260
be sitting there and I would forget that she wasn't you.

418
00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:44.220
Mm-hmm.

419
00:18:44.660 --> 00:18:47.460
Well, listen, this all happened on a Thursday night.

420
00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:50.780
By Saturday, Kent sent the whole cast this email.

421
00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:52.340
Saturday, April 12th.

422
00:18:52.460 --> 00:18:56.040
Hey, you guys, our one-liner schedule will be coming out later tomorrow.

423
00:18:56.520 --> 00:19:01.960
Please be advised that we are trying to shoot Miss Angela Kinsey out next week so she can go

424
00:19:01.960 --> 00:19:04.960
rest easily for a full week before delivering her little girl.

425
00:19:05.180 --> 00:19:09.340
And to accommodate this, Wednesday through Friday's schedule will be more grueling than

426
00:19:09.340 --> 00:19:11.780
normal, especially Friday night's work.

427
00:19:11.940 --> 00:19:13.740
Think Ferris wheel and fireworks.

428
00:19:14.140 --> 00:19:18.740
We will all take extra precautions to ensure Angela is comfortable and that she remains

429
00:19:18.740 --> 00:19:20.940
hydrated every single moment she is here.

430
00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:23.460
So prepare for the walkie-talkie chatter.

431
00:19:23.740 --> 00:19:25.840
Angela's going 10-1 again.

432
00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:31.960
So yeah, I almost didn't make it to the parking lot.

433
00:19:32.720 --> 00:19:34.040
Well, I'm glad you made it.

434
00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:35.060
I am too.

435
00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:39.100
I do remember the whole cast and crew were a little worried.

436
00:19:39.260 --> 00:19:39.880
We were concerned.

437
00:19:40.040 --> 00:19:44.900
We wanted to make sure that we got your work done first so that you could leave.

438
00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:45.380
Yes.

439
00:19:45.480 --> 00:19:47.420
And I left and Melissa Barker stayed.

440
00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:49.060
So thank you, Melissa Barker.

441
00:19:49.060 --> 00:19:54.420
And lady, now everyone is exiting the building, going into the parking lot.

442
00:19:54.820 --> 00:19:57.000
25 minutes, 52 seconds.

443
00:19:57.320 --> 00:19:58.060
Ugg alert.

444
00:19:58.700 --> 00:20:00.220
Who has the Uggs?

445
00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:03.180
Who has the warm, fuzzy Uggs on?

446
00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:04.420
Who is this person?

447
00:20:04.960 --> 00:20:05.680
It is me.

448
00:20:07.540 --> 00:20:11.420
And this starts a theme for this episode where they just gave up with me.

449
00:20:11.580 --> 00:20:13.260
They were like, just keep her comfortable.

450
00:20:13.260 --> 00:20:19.560
And I feel like in almost every shot, you can see my belly and I'm wearing Uggs and no one cares.

451
00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:20.580
You know what?

452
00:20:20.660 --> 00:20:25.000
I remember watching Seinfeld when Julia Louis-Dreyfus was pregnant.

453
00:20:25.060 --> 00:20:28.540
And there were a few times where I feel like it was the same.

454
00:20:28.820 --> 00:20:29.860
They were like, you know what?

455
00:20:29.860 --> 00:20:31.400
We all know she's pregnant.

456
00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:34.560
We're pretending like she's not pregnant because her character's not pregnant.

457
00:20:34.820 --> 00:20:37.360
Let's just, we're all in it together, folks.

458
00:20:37.660 --> 00:20:37.940
Yeah.

459
00:20:38.100 --> 00:20:39.280
We're just giving up.

460
00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:40.440
Exactly.

461
00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:45.680
Well, Michael is very disappointed that there is not an anti-gravity machine,

462
00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:47.980
but he is impressed with the Ferris wheel.

463
00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:49.080
Yeah.

464
00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:55.400
And there's a bouncy house, which by the way, poor Brian in the heat had to jump up and down

465
00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:56.520
in over and over.

466
00:20:56.620 --> 00:20:58.140
And it was so hot in there.

467
00:20:58.200 --> 00:21:03.840
And there's deleted scenes of him jumping and jumping and it didn't even make it in the episode.

468
00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:04.940
I know.

469
00:21:04.940 --> 00:21:09.840
So this is also when Pam clocks the fireworks and she realizes,

470
00:21:10.420 --> 00:21:13.160
oh my gosh, is Jim going to propose tonight?

471
00:21:13.400 --> 00:21:14.340
She's so excited.

472
00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:16.760
Lady, I thought you were so good in this episode.

473
00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:20.820
I thought your performance was so subtle and the emotion was so there.

474
00:21:20.820 --> 00:21:23.200
I just thought it was a beautiful, beautiful job.

475
00:21:23.420 --> 00:21:24.000
Oh my gosh.

476
00:21:24.180 --> 00:21:25.180
Thank you so much.

477
00:21:25.300 --> 00:21:25.660
Yeah.

478
00:21:25.660 --> 00:21:28.320
We had a fan question from Sophie F.

